/*
:name: nested_lambda_runtime_input
:type: error
:error: 'b' is a runtime value of the enclosing scope; it is not visible inside lambda 'addb'
:help: pass 'b' as an input of 'addb'
*/

// Ruling 2026-09-27 (suggestions 2.3 row 3): a nested lambda sees only
// COMPTIME bindings of its enclosing scopes (comptime const, generics,
// imports, types, lambdas). 06-functions.md: "Runtime `const`, `mut`, and
// `reg` declarations from enclosing lambda scopes are not visible inside a
// nested lambda unless passed as normal inputs". Reading the enclosing mod's
// RUNTIME input `b` inside the nested `comb addb` must be a compile error that
// tells the user to pass it as an input. Today it compiles with exit 0:
// prp2lnast turns `b` into a hidden closure input (streamed_lexical_names_)
// and the design silently computes `a + b`.
pub mod top(a:U8, b:U8) -> (o:U8@[0]) {
  comb addb(x:U8) -> (y:U8) {
    y = (x + b)#[0..<8]  // locate_error_here
  }
  o = addb(x=a)
}
